CM_ SG_ 942 REL_SPEED "Longitudinal speed relative to ego; negative means the target is moving longitudinally slower than ego.";
CM_ SG_ 942 NEW_SIGNAL_4 "Unknown category, observed 0-2. Zero dominates; 1/2 occur more often on moving targets.";
CM_ SG_ 942 REL_LAT_SPEED "Target lateral speed relative to the ego vehicle axis.";
CM_ SG_ 942 REL_ACCEL "Target longitudinal acceleration relative to ego acceleration.";
CM_ SG_ 942 NEW_SIGNAL_18 "Unknown optional measurement-status attribute. EV9/Ioniq 9 use 1/2 almost exclusively for measured STATE=3 tracks and 0 for coasted STATE=4 tracks; the distinction between 1 and 2 is unknown. The rare value 3 is also observed.";
CM_ SG_ 942 NEW_SIGNAL_5 "Unknown sparse optional attribute. Observed 0-32 and almost always 0; no stable correlation was found.";
CM_ SG_ 942 WIDTH "Strongly identified target width in 0.1 m units from recurring approximately 2.0 m passenger cars. Observed 0.0-3.0 m; many platforms transmit 0. Every address in the range can carry it.";
CM_ SG_ 942 LENGTH "Strongly identified target length in 0.1 m units from approximately 4.0 m cars and 13.0-15.5 m long vehicles. This is an 8-bit field; many platforms transmit 0.";
CM_ SG_ 942 ABS_SPEED "Strongly inferred absolute target-speed magnitude. On Ioniq 9 it matches hypot(ego speed + REL_SPEED, REL_LAT_SPEED), including targets without dimensions; observed 0.0-54.4 m/s.";
CM_ SG_ 942 ORIENTATION_ANGLE "Strongly inferred target orientation relative to the ego axis. Moving vehicles cluster near 0 degrees; it is associated with dimension-bearing targets. Values near +/-180 can be real rearward orientation on rich tracks, while non-rich platforms use +180 as an unavailable/default value.";
CM_ SG_ 942 NEW_SIGNAL_13 "Unknown optional 0-10 shape/geometry metric, nonzero only on dimension-bearing targets in tested routes.";
CM_ SG_ 942 NEW_SIGNAL_12 "Strong geometry-age/maturity candidate: two Ioniq 9 routes progressed 0, 1, 2, ... 10 and saturated at 10. Cross-platform confirmation is still insufficient for a semantic rename.";
CM_ SG_ 942 NEW_SIGNAL_14 "Unknown optional geometry category, observed 0-3. The common NEW_SIGNAL_14-17 tuple is 2,2,2,1.";
CM_ SG_ 942 NEW_SIGNAL_15 "Unknown optional geometry category, observed 0-2. The common NEW_SIGNAL_14-17 tuple is 2,2,2,1.";
CM_ SG_ 942 NEW_SIGNAL_16 "Unknown optional geometry category, observed 0-3. The common NEW_SIGNAL_14-17 tuple is 2,2,2,1.";
CM_ SG_ 942 NEW_SIGNAL_17 "Unknown optional geometry category, observed 0-2. The common NEW_SIGNAL_14-17 tuple is 2,2,2,1.";

